THE STABILITY CONCLUSION SURVIVES, and is now actually measured. All 16 configurations — the two
historical divergers g=8 n=3 and n=4, at dt=60 and at dt=1e20, with the momentum MG on and off,
at BOTH C/F schemes — reach the 400-step horizon finite. The cf=0 and cf=1 arms now differ, by
0.5 % (n=3, dt=60: 6.0439e+02 vs 6.0725e+02) and 1.7 % (n=4, dt=60: 5.9642e+02 vs 6.0697e+02),
which is the size of the C/F scheme's effect on these meshes and was invisible before.

The BASE (row-gate) arm of the cf=0 rows was NOT re-measured and does not need to be: at
cf=0 every buildCf*Delta returns an empty CSR before any gate is consulted
(`if (scheme == CfScheme::standard) return d;`), so the standard scheme is bit-identical on
`main` and on this branch by construction. The per-FACE gate can only move a cf=1 result.

The momMG rows remain pairwise identical (momentum MG on vs off) in every configuration, as they
were before the repair — that half of the bisection was never broken.


